From a3dd4b11e52a50d8aad81ee5ded9843bcd377675 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harshit Gupta <39994376+arelyx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 10:09:23 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/drm: flush once a growable ring holds more than 4
 MB

A long run of draws without a flush (piglit tex-miplevel-selection
bias shadow cases) grew the draw ring until the console had 38 MB
free; the xegpu low-memory guard then refused the next ring BO and
fd_ringbuffer_sp_grow mapped NULL. check_size now reports full past
4 MB so the batch flushes.

Generated-by: LLM
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QFJdrUq9L8NDS5PyGFCsG9
---
 src/freedreno/drm/freedreno_ringbuffer_sp.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/freedreno/drm/freedreno_ringbuffer_sp.c b/src/freedreno/drm/freedreno_ringbuffer_sp.c
index 7f50fcc..8bf2fca 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/drm/freedreno_ringbuffer_sp.c
+++ b/src/freedreno/drm/freedreno_ringbuffer_sp.c
@@ -714,6 +714,14 @@ fd_ringbuffer_sp_check_size(struct fd_ringbuffer *ring)
       return false;
    }
 
+   /* Bound the memory one growable ring can hold before a flush, so a
+    * long run of draws without a flush can't take all system RAM:
+    */
+   if ((ring->flags & FD_RINGBUFFER_GROWABLE) &&
+       (fd_ring->u.nr_cmds * ring->size > 4 * 1024 * 1024)) {
+      return false;
+   }
+
    return true;
 }
 
